{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator design direction (2026-08-10): do not retune the fuzzy low/medium/high boundary. Ordinal severity labels are an LLM anti-pattern because models do not apply those classifications reliably enough for deterministic gate behavior. Replace the undecomposed severity ladder with narrow semantic sub-questions whose answers map deterministically to blocking or advisory outcomes. Follow the pattern already used by the review pipeline for validation and impact: ask whether a specific condition is present (for example, required independently releasable work is missing from the decomposition versus an optional split would merely improve clarity), then apply the configured consequence in code. Reframe this ticket around explicit closed-set defect kinds and remove the grade-dependent proposal."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786394682136032001,"uuid":"4a13bc55-ef9b-41c8-8be6-2741dcd7fea2"}